---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = "";
---
<Base title="Cultural SEO: why an African & Black-owned brand needs an expert who knows its market" description="Cultural SEO isn't a slogan. It's a native understanding of the vocabulary, search intents and seasonality of the Black & African diaspora. Here's exactly what it changes." active="seo-culturel" jsonLd={jsonLd} lang="en" frPath="/seo-culturel/" enPath="/en/cultural-seo/">
<section class="hero hero--page wrap">
  <div class="hero-top">
    <span class="hero-eyebrow reveal"><img src="/images/icon-orange.png" alt="" /> The differentiator</span>
    <h1 class="reveal">"Cultural SEO" isn't a marketing angle.<br /><em>It's ground-level knowledge.</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub reveal">A generalist agency optimises keywords. I understand how <strong>your</strong> community searches — its words, its codes, its moments. Here's what that changes, concretely.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions reveal">
      <a href="https://calendly.com/contact-advised-seo/30min?back=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--orange">Book my Diagnostic
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 4 BLOCKS -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="kicker">What it means</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Four concrete proofs.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="feature-card reveal">
        <div class="fc-eyebrow"><span class="fc-num">01</span>The real vocabulary</div>
        <h3>The real vocabulary, not the generic keyword</h3>
        <p>Your customer doesn't search "hair shampoo" — she searches <em>"co-wash for 4C hair"</em>, <em>"low-poo routine"</em>, <em>"castor oil for type 4 hair growth"</em>, <em>"edge control for kinky hair"</em>. Your customer doesn't search "shoes" — he searches <em>"ankara trainers"</em>, <em>"made-in-Africa leather loafers"</em>. If your SEO ignores that vocabulary, you're invisible exactly where the buying intent lives.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card reveal">
        <div class="fc-eyebrow"><span class="fc-num">02</span>Missed intents</div>
        <h3>The intents generalists miss</h3>
        <p><em>"Dark spots on Black skin after a spot"</em>, <em>"buy hibiscus (zobo) tea online"</em>, <em>"where to buy egusi / fufu near me"</em>, <em>"loc maintenance routine"</em>… Strong intent, real volume — but off the radar for anyone who doesn't know the community.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card reveal">
        <div class="fc-eyebrow"><span class="fc-num">03</span>Seasonality</div>
        <h3>The seasons and the moments</h3>
        <p>The natural-hair journey, protective styles before summer, festival and wedding season, Detty December, back-to-school, community events: demand follows cycles you can't guess from a keyword spreadsheet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card reveal">
        <div class="fc-eyebrow"><span class="fc-num">04</span>AI visibility</div>
        <h3>Visibility in AI answers (GEO)</h3>
        <p>When someone asks ChatGPT <em>"best moisturiser for melanin-rich skin"</em> or <em>"haircare brand for type 4 hair"</em>, is it your brand that gets cited — or a competitor? GEO on diaspora queries is near-open ground. A lead to take now.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHY IT'S AN ADVANTAGE -->
<section class="sec offers">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal" style="max-width:860px">
      <span class="kicker">Why it's an advantage</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Your culture is a competitive advantage — as long as machines can read it.</h2>
      <p>An African &amp; Black-owned brand has a story, a community and a vocabulary that generic resellers will never own. Used well in SEO and GEO, those assets become a barrier to entry. Used badly, it's the soulless reseller who books the sale.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT IT IS NOT -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="note-band">
      <div class="note-card reveal">
        <span class="kicker">To be clear</span>
        <h3>What cultural SEO is not</h3>
        <p>It's not "classic SEO with an afro veneer". A community keyword stuck onto a generic strategy changes nothing about your visibility.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="note-card dark reveal">
        <span class="kicker">What it is</span>
        <h3>A rare intersection</h3>
        <p>The intersection of genuinely senior SEO expertise — technical, semantic, GEO — <strong>and</strong> a cultural fluency you can't improvise.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-band reveal">
      <img src="/images/icon-cream.png" class="icon-watermark" alt="" />
      <h2>Let's see what it looks like in your market.</h2>
      <p>The Diagnostic surfaces your high-potential community queries — and who's capturing them in your place today.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="https://calendly.com/contact-advised-seo/30min?back=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--orange">Book my Diagnostic
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/seo-diagnostic/" class="btn btn--cream">See the Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
